# text = He had no sooner been free from the horror and remorse attending the first few days of Louisa's accident , no sooner begun to feel himself alive again , than he had begun to feel himself , though alive , not at liberty said he He found too late , in short , that he had entangled himself ; and that precisely as he became fully satisfied of his not caring for Louisa at all , he must regard himself as bound to her , if her sentiments for him were what the Harvilles supposed .
